# netsurf: window.open opens a real popup window (claude.ai "Continue with Google")
#
# window.open was a same-realm stub (patch 125), so Google's sign-in popup
# never loaded. Now:
#
# - vita frontend: windows form a stack (window.c); a new one covers the one
#   it came from and closing it shows that one again. window.open
#   (js_platform.c macsurf_window_open) creates a top-level browser window
#   from the scheduler -- never inside the running script or mid main-loop
#   pass -- links its JS heap to the opener's (js_link_opener) and marks it
#   a popup. The page's window.close(), the opener's popup.close(), and L
#   (back) with no history left close it, also from the scheduler. The main
#   loop takes the top window's browser_window each pass.
# - bridge (macsurf_qjs.c): jsheap gains opener_heap + popup_id; natives
#   __vitaWindowOpen / __vitaPopupClosed / __vitaPopupClose /
#   __vitaCloseSelf / __vitaOpenerId / __vitaPostMessageToPopup /
#   __vitaPostMessageToOpener, over the same JSON-only queue as patch 126.
#   MessageEvent.origin is now scheme://host[:port] (was the full URL), and
#   event.source is the receiving realm's own shim for the sender (the
#   window window.open returned, iframe.contentWindow, parent, opener) when
#   it has one -- scripts compare them. Messages carry the sender's label.
# - polyfill: window.open returns a shim with postMessage / closed / close;
#   a popup realm gets window.opener and window.close; shims register in
#   __vitaShimWindows by label. Also iframe.sandbox and
#   link/a/area/form.relList as token lists over their attributes (Google's
#   sign-in module threw on iframe.sandbox.supports).
# - hit testing: a hoisted box with pointer-events: none lets the click
#   through to what is under it (Google's floating field label).
#
# Test page JS-popup.html (+ child): 4/4 in tools/run-vita-sim.sh (handle,
# source === handle, round trip, the popup closes itself and closed turns
# true). claude.ai in the simulator: "Continue with Google" opens
# accounts.google.com "Sign in to continue to Claude" in the popup and the
# email field takes typing.
